# Trivy accepted-findings allowlist (Q-5).
#
# The image scan (CRITICAL/HIGH, fixable-only) is a BLOCKING CI gate. When a
# finding is a genuine false positive or an accepted, time-boxed risk, add its
# CVE id here — ONE per line — with a comment stating WHY and a review date.
# Keep this list short and revisit every finding at its review date; an empty
# file means "block on everything fixable", which is the intended default.
#
# Format:
#   CVE-2024-XXXXX  # <why accepted> — review by YYYY-MM-DD

# jaraco.context 5.3.0 (path traversal) and wheel 0.45.1 (priv-esc) are
# BUILD-TIME packaging deps vendored inside setuptools/_vendor — not part of the
# app's runtime request path, and both HIGH (no CRITICAL). The proper fix is to
# strip pip/setuptools/wheel from the runtime image (they're only needed in the
# builder stage); that Dockerfile change needs a container build to verify and is
# tracked as a separate follow-up. Time-boxed accept until then.
CVE-2026-23949
# review by 2026-08-09 — jaraco.context, vendored in setuptools
CVE-2026-24049
# review by 2026-08-09 — wheel, vendored in setuptools (+ top-level)
